\section{Background and Related Work}
\label{sec:background}

\subsection{Merit-based sortition}
A pool of participants evolves over $N_{\mathrm{ep}}$ epochs. At epoch $i$ an active
set $A_i$ of size $N_{\mathrm{act}}$ (or the whole pool, if smaller) is fielded. Each active
participant $j$ produces an instantaneous quality $T_{ij}\sim\mathcal N(\tilde Q_j,V^2)$,
where the latent quality $\tilde Q_j\sim\mathcal N(\mu_Q,\sigma_Q^2)$ is fixed for the
participant's lifetime. Every participant carries a smoothed score
\begin{equation}\label{eq:ema}
Q_{ij}=\alpha\hat Q_{ij}+(1-\alpha)Q_{i-1,j},\;\;
\hat Q_{ij}=\begin{cases}T_{ij}, & j\in A_i,\\ f_P(T_{i,A_i}), & j\notin A_i,\end{cases}
\end{equation}
where $f_P$ is the $P$-th percentile of the active set's observations. The next active set
$A_{i+1}$ is the top $N_{\mathrm{act}}$ participants by $Q_{ij}$, with ties broken at
random. $P$ sets how optimistically unobserved participants are credited: a higher $P$
lifts inactive participants up the ranking and increases turnover.

We use the parameters of~\cite{kruijssen2024} throughout: $\mu_Q=0.2$, $\sigma_Q=0.1$,
$V=0.2$, $\alpha=0.1$, $N_{\mathrm{ep}}=1000$, and the four pool dynamics in
Table~\ref{tab:scenarios}. Growth is Poisson with rate $p_{\mathrm{growth}}$ per epoch,
and lifetimes are geometric with parameter $p_{\mathrm{attr}}$.

\paragraph{Experimental setup.} All experiments use a vectorised reimplementation of the
reference simulation. We validated it against a verbatim transcription of the loop-based
engine on $100$ seeds per configuration (four pools, fixed and adaptive $P$, both metrics
below). All $16$ comparisons are equivalent under two one-sided tests at the margin used
throughout the paper, with the largest mean difference $0.0015$. Each experiment draws its
own disjoint block of seeds. A run is $1000$ epochs, and its score is the time average of a
per-epoch metric. Code, per-seed results and scripts that regenerate every number and figure
will be released with the paper.

