\begin{remark}
There is also a reason in principle. $P$ sets the optimism credited to \emph{every}
unobserved participant alike, while the information that should govern optimism is
per participant: how long each has gone unobserved. A scalar control cannot carry it,
however it is computed. Per-participant exploration is a different mechanism, which we
study separately.
\end{remark}

